    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53272" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰρά̄τομ-ος</span></b>  (proparox.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέμνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beheaded</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γοργών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1118
				</span></i>
			 (dub.l.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐρημία
			νεανίδων</span>, i. e. their slaughter, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				564
			</span></i> (lyr.); so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἕκτορος . . κ. σφαγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					606
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>cut off from the head</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ.
			Χλιδαί</span> one's <i>shorn</i> locks, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				52
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> parox., 
				Act.
			, <i>beheading</i>, c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλλάδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					187
				</span></i>
			.</div>
